  "body": "Closes #1364\nClaim: cloud/i1364-sonnet\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5 (cloud/i1364-sonnet)\nReviewer model: Opus 5.5 (a8783eb1b204b6e88)\n\n## Problem\nThe operator's Xcode build of dev-swift shows 7 « main actor-isolated … from a nonisolated context » warnings in five app files (table on #1364).\n\n## Cause\n- `RowTint`, `ComposerHeader`, `MessageRowView` are `View`s, so their statics are main-actor by inference, yet pure value-type helpers (`ListLook.selectedStrength`, `MinimumHitRegion.overhang`, `MessageRowInfoLine.make`) call them.\n- `PagerToolbar` is not a `View`: its builders are nonisolated but build main-actor views (`PagerPageMenuPill.init`).\n- `TabBarReselectionObserver.Coordinator` was `@MainActor` while its `NSObject` overrides `responds(to:)` / `forwardingTarget(for:)` are nonisolated and read `previousDelegate`.\n\n## Change\n- `nonisolated` on the pure `RowTint.strength`, the constant `ComposerHeader.hitSize` and `MessageRowView.avatarSubject` (no main-actor state touched).\n- `@MainActor` on the view-building members of `PagerToolbar` (`toolbarContent`, `strip`, `stripRow`, `classicRow`, `statusView`), not on the struct: its memberwise init and `pageActions` are used from nonisolated tests (`PagerVisibilityTests`), which stay unchanged.\n- `Coordinator` is `nonisolated` as a type; its UIKit-touching members (`attach`, the two delegate methods, the static helpers) are `@MainActor` one by one; the two NSObject lookups only read the weak reference. No `@preconcurrency`, no `nonisolated(unsafe)`, no `assumeIsolated`. No behaviour change, no test edited.\n\n## Evidence\nCompile check (iOS 27 simulator, build-for-testing), job 140374525202, head 811e97d3: `** TEST BUILD SUCCEEDED **`.\n`grep -E 'warning:.*(ListLook|MinimumHitRegion|MessageRowInfoLine|PagerToolbar|TabBarReselectionObserver)'` on the job log: empty. The same grep widened to the touched `RowTint`/`ComposerHeader`/`MessageRowView` and to every `file.swift:l:c: warning` line: nothing in `App/SwiftHFR/`. Base log not compared (the issue's table is the \"before\").\nRemaining warnings in that log, outside this issue's five files (tests): `MessageTitleToneTests.swift:21-22` (`userInterfaceStyle`, `accessibilityContrast` mutated from nonisolated), `TopicRowCuesTests.swift:75` (`RowTint.overflow` in a nonisolated `#expect`), plus other `#expect` macro warnings. Not touched here (no test edit in this PR); worth their own issue.\n\nAdversarial review: APPROVE on 811e97d3 (comment above).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CEdAwSs6oRTio5P7ba",
