   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, adversarial reviewer a8783eb1b204b6e88, round 1): APPROVE** — head 811e97d3f1378ca299aa2be0f12bd1412f3d211f\n\nThe diff matches `origin/dev-swift...HEAD` exactly (5 files, +21/−16). It adds no `@preconcurrency`, no `nonisolated(unsafe)` and no `assumeIsolated`, changes no behaviour and touches no test.\n\n1. **Detail**, `App/SwiftHFR/Root/TabBarReselectionObserver.swift:79-81`. `responds(to:)` and `forwardingTarget(for:)` now read the weak `previousDelegate` without actor isolation, while the `@MainActor` method `attach` writes it. The type is not `Sendable`, so the compiler stops it from being shared across threads. A race could only come from the Objective-C runtime calling the delegate off the main thread, and UIKit does not do that. The doc comment says all this. No change needed.\n\nNo other findings:\n- **Statics on View types.** `RowTint.strength`, `ComposerHeader.hitSize` and `MessageRowView.avatarSubject` read only their arguments (Sendable values or `HFRModels` types) and constants; none uses main-actor state. Their callers, including the non-isolated tests, can only lose an isolation requirement.\n- **`PagerToolbar`.** The `@MainActor` chain is `statusView` ← `stripRow`/`classicRow` ← `strip` and `toolbarContent`. Their only callers are in `PagerBarModifier.body` (a `ViewModifier`, so on the main actor), in closures that take that isolation. `stripArrow` did not warn before and does not change.\n- **`TabBarReselectionObserver`.** The `@MainActor` delegate methods satisfy the main-actor requirements of `UITabBarControllerDelegate`, and the `NSObject` overrides stay non-isolated. `TabReselectHostedTests` is a `@MainActor` suite: the initializer, `attach`, the delegate calls and the `previousDelegate` reads all still type-check.\n\n**Verified**\n- `swiftlint lint` on the 5 files: clean. Longest added line is 136 characters, under the 140 limit.\n- A stand-in for the coordinator pattern, compiled with `swiftc 6.2.4 -swift-version 6 -strict-concurrency=complete -typecheck`: non-isolated subclass of a non-isolated base class, a `@MainActor` protocol with a `@MainActor` witness, a weak existential reference and overrides that read it. Result: 0 diagnostics.\n- With `@MainActor` back on that class (the old code), the same check gives exactly the 3 `previousDelegate` errors from the issue, so the change is what removes them (L01).\n- Same check for the statics: with `nonisolated` they compile clean; without it they give 4 diagnostics.\n- Limits: the stand-ins do not use UIKit or SwiftUI, and the app was not built. The CI job `App build + tests` has the final say on the acceptance grep for these warnings.\n\nReviewer model: Opus 5.5 (a8783eb1b204b6e88)\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
